WEBVTT

01-01
00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.511
Welcome to session four, solid equilibria and adsorption.

01-02
00:00:04.691 --> 00:00:10.621
This independent lesson replaces our live class while I attend the E C
S meeting.

01-03
00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:21.020
Last week, you used thermodynamic consistency and liquid stability to
decide whether a model and a proposed phase state were reasonable.

01-04
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.445
Today, we extend that reasoning to systems containing a solid.

01-05
00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:30.084
We will distinguish bulk phase equilibrium from surface uptake.

01-06
00:00:30.264 --> 00:00:38.413
We will also separate an equilibrium composition or pressure from the
amount of material in each part of a system.

01-07
00:00:38.593 --> 00:00:46.551
The lesson includes two actual Lab demonstrations, your own
calculations, and independent investigations.

01-08
00:00:46.731 --> 00:00:49.845
Keep your predictions and your first answers.

01-09
00:00:50.025 --> 00:00:55.551
Correcting an explanation after checking evidence is an important part
of the work.

02-01
00:00:58.081 --> 00:01:04.673
Open the six-page practice worksheet and the four-page Lab guide using
the links on this slide.

02-02
00:01:04.853 --> 00:01:06.773
Keep both beside the video.

02-03
00:01:06.953 --> 00:01:13.971
The worksheet is your working record, while the guide tells you which
controls to use and what each result means.

02-04
00:01:14.151 --> 00:01:21.550
The worked solutions are available for checking, but attempt each
question before opening the corresponding answer.

02-05
00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:28.002
Keep your original response and add a correction, rather than
replacing it without explanation.

02-06
00:01:28.182 --> 00:01:34.731
You will first work through Lab ten on bulk solid equilibria, then Lab
eleven on adsorption.

02-07
00:01:34.911 --> 00:01:41.546
The demonstrations show the workflow, and the later pauses give you
time to reproduce it independently.

02-08
00:01:41.726 --> 00:01:48.446
Save your calculation sheets, comparison tables and study J S O N
files together.

03-01
00:01:50.976 --> 00:01:54.112
This route combines watching with active work.

03-02
00:01:54.292 --> 00:01:59.817
The fixed work budget is one hundred and twenty minutes, with a
separate ten-minute break.

03-03
00:01:59.997 --> 00:02:04.136
The actual recording duration appears on the video page.

03-04
